-- 100 real words across 5 topics, all inside the QA fixture's existing group
-- ("QA Isolation Test Class", 011_qa_test_tenant_seed.sql) — bulk sample
-- content for qa.admin@dygo.test to browse, on top of that file's bare
-- tenant/group/membership scaffold. Generated from database/migrations/
-- ../../../tmp/qa_seed/{words_data,generate_sql}.py (not checked in — the SQL
-- below is the artifact that matters; the generator just avoided hand-typing
-- 100 INSERT rows and getting an apostrophe-escape wrong somewhere in them).
--
-- Every word is a genuine dictionary entry — real IPA, CEFR level, a correct
-- one-line definition, synonyms/antonyms with their own levels, and one example
-- sentence — not placeholder text. All 100 are status = 'READY' (fully enriched)
-- since the point here is volume to browse, not exercising ENRICHING/FAILED —
-- those states already have real coverage on Sarah's fixtures (004_seed_data.sql).
--
-- LOADING: independent of 004 and 011 in the sense that it only adds rows, but
-- it FOREIGN-KEYS onto 011's group and admin user, so 011 must be loaded first.
--   ./database/apply-migrations.sh --qa-seed-only        # 011, if not already loaded
--   ./database/apply-migrations.sh --qa-words-seed-only  # this file
-- Safe to re-run: every insert is ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING/UPDATE.
